From: Luigi Pavan <lpavan@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glnx/chase: Tolerate missing STATX_MNT_ID on older kernels

RHEL 8 / CentOS Stream 8 kernels (4.18-based) implement statx(2) but do
not return STATX_MNT_ID / STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE (those landed in Linux 5.8).
Bundled libglnx's glnx_chase_statx() currently treats a missing mount id
as a hard error:

  error: statx didn't return all required fields: No data available

That failure is hit on every flatpak run after the CVE-2026-90616 backport
switches ensure_data_dir / /var setup to glnx_chase_and_mkdirat(), because
the mkdir callback forces the openat2-less chase_manual() path:

  flatpak run
    -> flatpak_builtin_run
      -> flatpak_run_app
        -> flatpak_ensure_data_dir
          -> glnx_chase_and_mkdirat (callback = chase_and_mkdir)
            -> glnx_chaseat_full  (skips openat2: callback != NULL)
              -> chase_manual
                -> glnx_chase_statx (root_fd)
                  -> ENODATA / "statx didn't return all required fields"

Relax the check: still require TYPE and INO, but allow missing mount id.
When comparing mounts in glnx_statx_mount_same(), prefer mount id when
present; otherwise fall back to stx_dev_major/stx_dev_minor. Device
identity is coarser than mount id (bind mounts of the same superblock
share st_dev), but creating such mounts requires mount privilege that a
sandboxed Flatpak app does not have. The GHSA-8688-9x26-hhxj defense
(RESOLVE_BENEATH + --bind-fd against escape symlinks) remains intact.

Assisted-by: Cursor
---
 subprojects/libglnx/glnx-chase.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/subprojects/libglnx/glnx-chase.c
+++ b/subprojects/libglnx/glnx-chase.c
@@ -104,10 +104,17 @@
 glnx_statx_mount_same (const struct glnx_statx *a,
                        const struct glnx_statx *b)
 {
-  g_assert ((a->stx_mask & (GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID | GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE)) != 0);
-  g_assert ((b->stx_mask & (GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID | GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE)) != 0);
+  /* Prefer mount id when the kernel provides it (Linux 5.8+). */
+  if ((a->stx_mask & (GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID | GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE)) != 0 &&
+      (b->stx_mask & (GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID | GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE)) != 0)
+    return a->stx_mnt_id == b->stx_mnt_id;
 
-  return a->stx_mnt_id == b->stx_mnt_id;
+  /* Older kernels (e.g. RHEL 8 / 4.18) implement statx but not STATX_MNT_ID.
+   * Fall back to filesystem device identity. This is coarser than mount id
+   * (bind mounts of the same superblock share st_dev) but is sufficient for
+   * flatpak's ensure_data_dir /var setup under ~/.var/app. */
+  return a->stx_dev_major == b->stx_dev_major &&
+         a->stx_dev_minor == b->stx_dev_minor;
 }
 
 static gboolean
@@ -124,9 +131,13 @@
                    error))
     return FALSE;
 
+  /* TYPE and INO are required. Mount id is optional: kernels before Linux 5.8
+   * (including RHEL 8) may omit STATX_MNT_ID / STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE. Without
+   * this fallback, flatpak run fails with:
+   *   error: statx didn't return all required fields: No data available
+   */
   if ((buf->stx_mask & (GLNX_STATX_TYPE | GLNX_STATX_INO)) !=
-        (GLNX_STATX_TYPE | GLNX_STATX_INO) ||
-      (buf->stx_mask & (GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID | GLNX_STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE)) == 0)
+        (GLNX_STATX_TYPE | GLNX_STATX_INO))
     {
       errno = ENODATA;
       return glnx_throw_errno_prefix (error,
